DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These  functions  are  used to simplify analysis of memory leaks in the
       _n_c_u_r_s_e_s library.

       Any implementation of curses must not free the memory associated with a
       screen, since (even after calling eennddwwiinn(3X)), it must be available for
       use in the next call to rreeffrreesshh(3X).  There are also chunks  of  memory
       held for performance reasons.  That makes it hard to analyze curses ap‐
       plications for memory leaks.  When using the specially  configured  de‐
       bugging version of the _n_c_u_r_s_e_s library, applications can call functions
       which free those chunks of memory, simplifying the process  of  memory-
       leak checking.

       Some  of  the functions are named with a “_nc_” prefix because they are
       not intended for use in the non-debugging library:

       __nncc__ffrreeeeaallll
            This frees (almost) all of the memory allocated by _n_c_u_r_s_e_s.

       __nncc__ffrreeee__aanndd__eexxiitt
            This frees the memory allocated by _n_c_u_r_s_e_s (like __nncc__ffrreeeeaallll), and
            exits the program.  It is preferred over __nncc__ffrreeeeaallll since some of
            that memory may be required to keep the application running.  Sim‐
            ply exiting (with the given exit-code) is safer.

       __nncc__ffrreeee__ttiinnffoo
            Use  this  function  if only the low-level terminfo functions (and
            corresponding library) are used.  Like __nncc__ffrreeee__aanndd__eexxiitt, it exits
            the program after freeing memory.

       The  functions  prefixed “_nc” are normally not available; they must be
       configured into the library at build time using the ----ddiissaabbllee--lleeaakkss op‐
       tion.   That compiles-in code that frees memory that normally would not
       be freed.

       The eexxiitt__ccuurrsseess and eexxiitt__tteerrmmiinnffoo functions call __nncc__ffrreeee__aanndd__eexxiitt  and
       __nncc__ffrreeee__ttiinnffoo  if  the  library  is  configured to support memory-leak
       checking.  If the library is  not  configured  to  support  memory-leak
       checking, they simply call eexxiitt.

